  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Samuel",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "David learns of the death of Saul and Jonathan—He slays the Amalekite who claims to have killed Saul—David laments the passing of Saul and Jonathan with a song.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now it came to pass after the death of Saul, when David was returned from the slaughter of the Amalekites, and David had abode two days in Ziklag;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:1",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "It came even to pass on the third day, that, behold, a man came out of the camp from Saul with his clothes rent, and earth upon his head: and so it was, when he came to David, that he fell to the earth, and did obeisance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 144
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:2",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said unto him, From whence comest thou? And he said unto him, Out of the camp of Israel am I escaped.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:3",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said unto him, How went the matter? I pray thee, tell me. And he answered, That the people are fled from the battle, and many of the people also are fallen and dead; and Saul and Jonathan his son are dead also.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:4",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said unto the young man that told him, How knowest thou that Saul and Jonathan his son be dead?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:5",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And the young man that told him said, As I happened by chance upon mount Gilboa, behold, Saul leaned upon his spear; and, lo, the chariots and horsemen followed hard after him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:6",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he looked behind him, he saw me, and called unto me. And I answered, Here am I.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 85
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:7",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said unto me, Who art thou? And I answered him, I am an Amalekite.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:8",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "He said unto me again, Stand, I pray thee, upon me, and slay me: for anguish is come upon me, because my life is yet whole in me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 112
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:9",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "So I stood upon him, and slew him, because I was sure that he could not live after that he was fallen: and I took the crown that was upon his head, and the bracelet that was on his arm, and have brought them hither unto my lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "1 Sam. 31:4 (1–4); 1 Chr. 10:4 (4–5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 132
          },
          {
            "start": 170,
            "end": 173
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:10",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Then David took hold on his clothes, and rent them; and likewise all the men that were with him:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:11",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And they mourned, and wept, and fasted until even, for Saul, and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the Lord, and for the house of Israel; because they were fallen by the sword.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:12",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said unto the young man that told him, Whence art thou? And he answered, I am the son of a stranger, an Amalekite.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:13",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said unto him, How wast thou not afraid to stretch forth thine hand to destroy the Lord’s anointed?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "2 Sam. 4:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "TG Anointing."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 4:10.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 4:10",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
