        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:18",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The beauty of Israel is slain upon thy high places: how are the mighty fallen!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:19",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Tell it not in Gath, publish it not in the streets of Askelon; lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:20",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye mountains of Gilboa, let there be no dew, neither let there be rain, upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Saul, as though he had not been anointed with oil.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 199
          },
          {
            "start": 204,
            "end": 208
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:21",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the mighty, the bow of Jonathan turned not back, and the sword of Saul returned not empty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:22",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Saul and Jonathan were lovely and pleasant in their lives, and in their death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, they were stronger than lions.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "D&C 135:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 22
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 135:3.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 135:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 135,
                    "end": 135,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Samuel 1:23",
        "book": "Samuel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye daughters of Israel, weep over Saul, who clothed you in scarlet, with other delights, who put on ornaments of gold upon your apparel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 135,
            "text": "TG Prosperity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
